receiver_slot.parity:
All parity runs use budget_s=None, and the budget logic is checked on a fake clock (seams.now / a stubbed receiver.time.monotonic).

Bit-exact:
- the rules (_aliases, _ghosts, _ghost_of, _suspect_neighbour, _suspect_beside, _a3_lines, _owned) over a 600-seed fuzz, with GATING both ways;
- detection lists given back by identity;
- headers and cw;
- the stubbed orchestration fuzz: 2000 worlds, CE and joint, about 49k stage calls, identical call logs (stage, argument and order, budget `taken += 1` before the merge skip, max_candidates, skip_hz, hints, erase_s), with every rule branch hit at least 8 times;
- the budget stopping at exactly the reference candidate;
- capture_from_wav bitwise against native audio_to_fe(wavio.read_wav) for 8/16/24/32-bit int, float32/64, extensible GUID, LIST chunks and multichannel;
- typed mode against Python mode inside the binding, on every scenario.

Tolerance (bar / measured worst):
- detect: f_hz 1e-6 Hz / 0; tau0 1e-6 s / 4.6e-12 CH samples; z_ref 1e-6 rel / 1.1e-7; ppm 6.0e-10; path 3e-16.
- receive_slot: f_hz 1.8e-12 Hz; tau0 2.4e-12 CH samples; z 9.4e-10 rel to scale and 7.1e-8 elementwise; w 0; cw z_match 0; report z_ref 1.1e-7; everything else under 1e-10.
- These held over 18 scenarios: CE tiny, L tiny, joint, CE beside L, alias, weak neighbour, noise, old-gating, old-edge-noise, live-only, max-candidates CE and joint, erase, hints, plain estimator, and SHORT CE/L/joint.
- Erased passes are the one exception: z_ref reached 1.06e-6 against a 1e-5 bar (_erased_same), because the erased-segment z_ref inherits the Kalman P conditioning (see insights).
- _ce_resid_ratio: 1e-12 relative on real CE and L tracks.
- capture_from_wav at resampled rates: 1e-12 against native, 1e-5 against the reference.
- Whole callers, with spies installed before the rows: qrss_receive.py main (npz joint and WAV --slot --frame tiny --just-ce --no-store) and live.finish_receive. Reference, counted (spy, Python mode) and typed runs were compared on everything except the uid hash, and every _SLOT_ROWS entry was asserted reached.

Not compared:
- the wall-clock budget against a real clock (only the fake clock);
- FULL-frame scenarios (timed only);
- the acceptance suite (slow, CLI subprocesses).

